+      "key": "finite-determinantal-entropy-concavity-implies-stationary-entropy-rate-concavity",
+      "namespace": "probability.determinantal",
+      "logical_name": "finite-determinantal-entropy-concavity-implies-stationary-entropy-rate-concavity",
+      "kind": "lemma",
+      "title": "Finite determinantal entropy concavity implies stationary entropy-rate concavity",
+      "statement": "PROOF OF THE STATED SCOPED RESULT; independent audit pending. If Shannon entropy of finite determinantal measures is midpoint-concave in the positive-contraction kernel for every finite set, then the entropy rate of stationary determinantal processes on Z is midpoint-concave in their measurable [0,1]-valued circle symbols. Finite restrictions are linear in the symbol; dividing their inequalities by the interval length and taking the subadditive entropy-rate limit proves the implication. No converse is asserted, and the fixed-diagonal two-site lemma does not supply the premise for all sizes.",
+      "proof_text": "# C0033: the conditional implication has one direction\n\nLabel: proof of a conditional implication, awaiting w346. This continues the corrected C0033-A002 record, without proving its premise.\n\nAssume finite-kernel determinantal entropy is midpoint-concave for every finite index set. Let f,g be measurable symbols on the circle with values in [0,1], and let P_f,P_g be their stationary determinantal processes on Z. Their N-coordinate kernels are linear in the symbols, so the kernel of the restriction for (f+g)/2 is the arithmetic mean of the two restricted kernels. The assumption gives H_N(P_((f+g)/2)) >= [H_N(P_f)+H_N(P_g)]/2.\n\nFor every stationary binary process, H_N is subadditive: H_(N+M)<=H_N+H_M by the entropy chain rule and stationarity. Fekete's lemma therefore gives a limit h(P)=lim H_N(P)/N, with 0<=h(P)<=log(2). Divide the finite inequality by N and take the limits to obtain h(P_((f+g)/2)) >= [h(P_f)+h(P_g)]/2.\n\nThus the full finite-kernel conjecture implies the stationary entropy-rate conjecture. This argument supplies no converse; the old store wording \"equivalently\" is not justified by it. The newly proved fixed-diagonal two-site result also does not establish the premise for all N.\n",
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Finite-kernel concavity is assumed at every size",
+        "Stationary binary determinantal processes with symbols in [0,1]"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability theory",
